                                       target=\"_blank\"\n                                       class=\"btn view-btn btn-sm\">\n                                        View Brochure\n                                    <\/a>\n                                \n                                <a target=\"_blank\"\n                                   href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/seo-course?utm_source=WsBlog&#038;utm_medium=blog_course_slider&#038;utm_campaign=SEO\"\n                                   class=\"btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm\">\n                                    Learn More\n                                <\/a>\n                            <\/div>\n                        <\/div>\n                    <\/div>\n\n                \n            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/section>\n\n    \n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Top 10 Social Media Platforms in India<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>If you are looking for the&nbsp;top 10 social media platforms in India, here is the current lineup, ranked by estimated users in the country. This list includes WhatsApp because, despite being a messaging app, most Indians treat it as their primary social platform.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">1. WhatsApp<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"224\" height=\"225\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/whatsapp.webp\" alt=\"WhatsApp\" class=\"wp-image-21752\" style=\"width:150px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/whatsapp.webp 224w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/whatsapp-150x150.webp 150w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 224px) 100vw, 224px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p>WhatsApp is the single most used app in India, with around&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/richautomate.in\/blog\/whatsapp-users-india-2026-statistics\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">535.8 million<\/a>&nbsp;users.&nbsp;It is used for personal chats, family groups, and increasingly for small business communication through WhatsApp Business.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">2. YouTube<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"310\" height=\"163\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/03\/youtube.webp\" alt=\"YouTube\" class=\"wp-image-7940\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/03\/youtube.webp 310w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/03\/youtube-300x158.webp 300w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/03\/youtube-150x79.webp 150w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 310px) 100vw, 310px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p>YouTube reaches about&nbsp;500 million users&nbsp;in India, as reported by&nbsp;DataReportal. It&nbsp;is&nbsp;the&nbsp;go-to platform for entertainment, education, tutorials, and long-form video content.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">3. Instagram<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"148\" height=\"148\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/05\/instagram-logo.webp\" alt=\"Instagram\" class=\"wp-image-19231\" style=\"width:180px;height:auto\"\/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p>Instagram has around&nbsp;481 million users&nbsp;in&nbsp;India. It&nbsp;remains&nbsp;the top choice for photo sharing, Reels, influencer marketing, and brand storytelling.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">4. Facebook<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"866\" height=\"650\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/03\/facebook.webp\" alt=\"Facebook\" class=\"wp-image-7937\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1.3323089886248172;width:204px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/03\/facebook.webp 866w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/03\/facebook-300x225.webp 300w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/03\/facebook-768x576.webp 768w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/03\/facebook-150x113.webp 150w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 866px) 100vw, 866px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p>Facebook still holds&nbsp;a strong base&nbsp;of&nbsp;403 million users&nbsp;in India. It is&nbsp;widely used for community groups, local buy-and-sell marketplaces, and older demographics.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">5.&nbsp;ShareChat<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"436\" height=\"234\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/sharechat.webp\" alt=\"ShareChat\" class=\"wp-image-21753\" style=\"width:294px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/sharechat.webp 436w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/sharechat-300x161.webp 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 436px) 100vw, 436px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p>ShareChat, a homegrown app, has crossed&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/ShareChat\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">350 million<\/a>&nbsp;monthly active users, as&nbsp;noted on&nbsp;Wikipedia. It focuses on regional language content across more than 15 Indian languages.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">6. Snapchat<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"225\" height=\"225\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/snapchat.webp\" alt=\"Snapchat\" class=\"wp-image-21754\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/snapchat.webp 225w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/snapchat-150x150.webp 150w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 225px) 100vw, 225px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p>Snapchat has around&nbsp;213 million users&nbsp;in India, based&nbsp;on&nbsp;DataReportal&nbsp;data. It&nbsp;remains&nbsp;popular among younger users for its camera filters and disappearing content.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">7. LinkedIn<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1400\" height=\"362\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/03\/linkedin.webp\" alt=\"Linkedin\" class=\"wp-image-7939\" style=\"aspect-ratio:3.86428982173663;width:322px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/03\/linkedin.webp 1400w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/03\/linkedin-300x78.webp 300w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/03\/linkedin-1024x265.webp 1024w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/03\/linkedin-768x199.webp 768w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/03\/linkedin-150x39.webp 150w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1400px) 100vw, 1400px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p>LinkedIn counts about&nbsp;170 million members&nbsp;in India. It is&nbsp;the leading platform for professional networking, hiring, and career growth.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">8. Moj<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"172\" height=\"159\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/moj.webp\" alt=\"Moj\" class=\"wp-image-21755\"\/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p>Moj, developed by&nbsp;ShareChat, has over&nbsp;160 million monthly active users.&nbsp;It offers short-video content in multiple Indian languages and grew rapidly after TikTok was banned in India.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">9. Telegram<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"447\" height=\"447\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/telegram.webp\" alt=\"Telegram\" class=\"wp-image-21756\" style=\"width:171px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/telegram.webp 447w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/telegram-300x300.webp 300w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/telegram-150x150.webp 150w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 447px) 100vw, 447px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p>Telegram has close to&nbsp;104 million users&nbsp;in India. It is known for large broadcast channels, file sharing, and group communication.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">10. Facebook Messenger<\/h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"447\" height=\"447\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/facebook-messenger.webp\" alt=\"Facebook Messenger\" class=\"wp-image-21757\" style=\"width:187px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/facebook-messenger.webp 447w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/facebook-messenger-300x300.webp 300w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/facebook-messenger-150x150.webp 150w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 447px) 100vw, 447px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p>Messenger reaches around&nbsp;108 million users&nbsp;in India. It&nbsp;is mostly used alongside Facebook for direct chats and quick replies to businesses.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>This list of the&nbsp;best social media app in India&nbsp;options shows a mix of messaging tools, video platforms, and regional apps, which reflects how diverse the country&#8217;s internet users really are.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Top Social Media Platforms in India (2026 Data)<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Beyond the top names, there are several other apps that hold a meaningful place in India&#8217;s digital space. Below is a broader&nbsp;list of social media platforms in India, covering both major and smaller players.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td><strong>Rank<\/strong>&nbsp;<\/td><td><strong>App<\/strong>&nbsp;<\/td><td><strong>Estimated Users in India<\/strong>&nbsp;<\/td><td><strong>Primary Use<\/strong>&nbsp;<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1&nbsp;<\/td><td><a href=\"https:\/\/web.whatsapp.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">WhatsApp<\/a><\/td><td>535.8 million&nbsp;<\/td><td>Messaging, calls, business chat&nbsp;<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>2&nbsp;<\/td><td><a href=\"https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">YouTube<\/a><\/td><td>500 million&nbsp;<\/td><td>Video streaming, education&nbsp;<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>3&nbsp;<\/td><td><a href=\"https:\/\/www.instagram.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Instagram<\/a>&nbsp;<\/td><td>481 million&nbsp;<\/td><td>Photos, Reels, influencer content&nbsp;<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>4&nbsp;<\/td><td><a href=\"https:\/\/www.facebook.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Facebook<\/a><\/td><td>403 million&nbsp;<\/td><td>Groups, marketplace, community&nbsp;<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>5&nbsp;<\/td><td><a href=\"https:\/\/sharechat.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">ShareChat<\/a><\/td><td>350 million&nbsp;<\/td><td>Regional language content&nbsp;<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>6&nbsp;<\/td><td><a href=\"https:\/\/www.snapchat.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Snapchat<\/a><\/td><td>213 million&nbsp;<\/td><td>Camera filters, youth content&nbsp;<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>7&nbsp;<\/td><td><a href=\"https:\/\/www.linkedin.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">LinkedIn<\/a><\/td><td>170 million&nbsp;<\/td><td>Professional networking, jobs&nbsp;<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>8&nbsp;<\/td><td><a href=\"https:\/\/mojapp.in\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Moj<\/a><\/td><td>160 million&nbsp;<\/td><td>Short-video entertainment&nbsp;<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>9&nbsp;<\/td><td><a href=\"https:\/\/www.messenger.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Messenger<\/a><\/td><td>108 million&nbsp;<\/td><td>Chat and business messaging&nbsp;<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>10&nbsp;<\/td><td><a href=\"https:\/\/web.telegram.org\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Telegram<\/a><\/td><td>104 million&nbsp;<\/td><td>Group broadcasts, file sharing&nbsp;<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>11&nbsp;<\/td><td><a href=\"https:\/\/www.threads.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Threads<\/a><\/td><td>26.6 million&nbsp;<\/td><td>Text-based microblogging&nbsp;<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>12&nbsp;<\/td><td><a href=\"https:\/\/www.reddit.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Reddit<\/a><\/td><td>30.8 million&nbsp;<\/td><td>Discussion forums, communities&nbsp;<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>13&nbsp;<\/td><td><a href=\"https:\/\/x.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">X (Twitter)<\/a><\/td><td>22.2 million&nbsp;<\/td><td>News, real-time updates&nbsp;<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>14&nbsp;<\/td><td><a href=\"https:\/\/myjosh.in\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Josh<\/a><\/td><td>Tens of millions&nbsp;<\/td><td>Regional short-video content&nbsp;<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>15&nbsp;<\/td><td><a href=\"https:\/\/chingari.io\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Chingari<\/a><\/td><td>Millions&nbsp;<\/td><td>Video sharing with rewards&nbsp;<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>16&nbsp;<\/td><td><a href=\"https:\/\/www.pinterest.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Pinterest<\/a><\/td><td>Millions&nbsp;<\/td><td>Visual discovery, inspiration&nbsp;<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>17&nbsp;<\/td><td><a href=\"https:\/\/discord.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Discord<\/a><\/td><td>Millions&nbsp;<\/td><td>Community and gaming chat&nbsp;<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>18&nbsp;<\/td><td><a href=\"https:\/\/quora.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Quora<\/a><\/td><td>Millions&nbsp;<\/td><td>Question-and-answer forum&nbsp;<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-white-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-background-color has-text-color has-background has-link-color wp-elements-da6a587ca57f453b99af6c1dac82bdc9\"><strong><em>Note:<\/em><\/strong><em>&nbsp;figures marked &#8220;millions&#8221; do not have a recent, verified country-level count and should be treated as approximate.<\/em><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Covering&nbsp;all social media platforms in India&nbsp;in one place is tricky because user numbers change often and companies do not always share exact figures for every country. Even so, this table gives a fair picture of where Indian users&nbsp;actually spend&nbsp;their time. For brands trying to keep track of activity across so many apps, using proper&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/social-media-management-tools\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">social media management tools<\/a>&nbsp;can make&nbsp;a big difference&nbsp;in staying&nbsp;organized&nbsp;and consistent.<\/p>\n\n\n\n        <div class=\"container position-relative mb-2\">\n            <div class=\"row pb-4\">\n                <h2 style=\"font-size:32px\">Upcoming Masterclass<\/h2>